ature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T13:31:36-07:00","id":1413829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413803#post1413803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda hope they don't, because even leaving out all the creepy sex stuff that is only creepier with some of the controversies surrounding Bradley's life (but still, make a note of those), the book still isn't very good, not even at its nominal goal of &amp;quot;Arthur Myth but girl power version!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember a couple of &quot;Arthurian Myth but girl power version!&quot; fantasy novels from the early 70s. Some of them were fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T13:33:09-07:00","id":1413831,"title":"","content":"Really hoping that 1) the Welsh pantheon is in there; and 2) they get as much limelight as the Arthurian mythos in there.<br /> Bonus points if the conflicting tales are due to multiple Arthurs trying to claim (and complete) the mantle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T14:19:51-07:00","id":1413837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413803#post1413803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda hope they don't, because even leaving out all the creepy sex stuff that is only creepier with some of the controversies surrounding Bradley's life (but still, make a note of those), the book still isn't very good, not even at its nominal goal of &quot;Arthur Myth but girl power version!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I know all about the controversy, and my skin still crawls when I think about it, but that doesn\u2019t change the fact that the book itself is really good. I read it when I was like 7 and it basically set the standard in my mind for what an Arthurian fantasy should be like (idk anything about the controversy till years later when I was a lot older).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-15-2020, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T14:23:54-07:00","id":1413839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413831#post1413831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really hoping that 1) the Welsh pantheon is in there; and 2) they get as much limelight as the Arthurian mythos in there.<br /> Bonus points if the conflicting tales are due to multiple Arthurs trying to claim (and complete) the mantle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T15:22:04-07:00","id":1413855,"title":"","content":"That was always Merlyn\u2019s plan of course. To guarantee that an Arthur could always arise when needed the story must always end in tragedy, the Mantle incomplete, so that someone else can rise to walk the path again when needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T17:42:06-07:00","id":1413876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413767#post1413767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably an Arthurian book. I hope they use The Mists of Avalon as inspiration. But at the risk of repeating myself, even if they don\u2019t, that is so awesome!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>My sister saw that book on the kitchen table after I got it from the Science Fiction Book Club. She confiscated it by her &quot;authority&quot; as the big sister (then as now I tower over her) and I never got to read the book. I saw it again a few years later when we visited her in Virginia Beach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T18:56:29-07:00","id":1413886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413876#post1413876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My sister saw that book on the kitchen table after I got it from the Science Fiction Book Club. She confiscated it by her &amp;quot;authority&amp;quot; as the big sister (then as now I tower over her) and I never got to read the book. I saw it again a few years later when we visited her in Virginia Beach.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should get it on Amazon. You\u2019ll totally love it, if you\u2019re into that kind of thing. It\u2019s basically a \u201cgirl power\u201d reinterpretation of the Arthurian Cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T19:51:07-07:00","id":1413893,"title":"","content":"Perhaps purchase the book from a used bookstore if you must, because MZB's daughter did come out and make very clear that her mother was involved in sexually abusing her and other children for years. <br /> <br /> I can't speak for anyone else, but that's definitely not on my 'suggested Arthurian media' list. There is at least one very clear depiction of a child being raped under the auspices of a pagan ritual in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T20:02:25-07:00","id":1413894,"title":"","content":"I wonder if good ol merlin will show up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T22:06:15-07:00","id":1413908,"title":"","content":"Demigod book mentions Arthur as one ALMOST getting to Godhood? Interesting would be to read on that in terms of Scion...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T22:12:22-07:00","id":1413909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413894#post1413894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if good ol merlin will show up</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd expect at the very least a biography and Merlin statted up as a Guide. Maybe take a moment to talk about just how many backstories Merlin has. There's probably been quite a few people who went by Merlin. If I were on the writing team I'd probably say he's a Sorcerer, and depending on how far Saints and Monsters is in development I may go &quot;For full Sorcerer rules see Saints and Monsters&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T23:10:17-07:00","id":1413918,"title":"","content":"That sounds very plausible!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T09:41:32-07:00","id":1413979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413909#post1413909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd expect at the very least a biography and Merlin statted up as a Guide. Maybe take a moment to talk about just how many backstories Merlin has. There's probably been quite a few people who went by Merlin. If I were on the writing team I'd probably say he's a Sorcerer, and depending on how far Saints and Monsters is in development I may go &quot;For full Sorcerer rules see Saints and Monsters&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As some portrayals give Merlyn supernatural parentage, I wouldn't ruleout a Scion created Mantle floating around as well. Maybe Sorcerers will have a way to at least temporarily harness Mantles through ritual emulation. Seems plausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T11:49:29-07:00","id":1413994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413893#post1413893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps purchase the book from a used bookstore if you must, because MZB's daughter did come out and make very clear that her mother was involved in sexually abusing her and other children for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. About ten years ago, I decided to correct the fact that I'd really not read any of the mass of Arthurian inspired fiction out there, and Mists of Avalon is really the only major/well known one I didn't read just because I could never find it at my local used bookstore. (This was even before I heard about the allegations against her.)<br /> <br /> As for other stuff:<br /> <br /> I have some vague recollections of seeing Disney's<i> The Sword and the Stone</i> as a kid in the very early 80s, but my biggest memory of being exposed to Arthurian myth as a kid was seeing John Boorman's <b>Excalibur</b> on TV. Even though a fair bit of it went over my head, it was still visually striking enough to leave an impact. (A few years later, <b>Sword of the Valiant</b> was on TV at my grandparents' house one Sunday afternoon, but we had to leave to go home right after Sean Connery's Green Knight puts his head back on after Gawain cut it off, and it took me nearly two decades to finally find out what movie that was and find it for rent so I could actually see the end of it.) I also remember enjoying reading Prince Valiant each week in the Sunday newspaper comic strips. (Newspapers are these things that people used to get on a regular basis for ... never mind.)<br /> <br /> My decision to start playing catch up with Arthurian fiction was sparked by my late aunt (the other major reader in the family) giving me a copy of <b>Mary Stewart's Merlin Trilogy</b> (The Crystal Cave, The Hollow Hills, and The Last Enchantment), which are really good and I do recommend them, as well as her follow up book about Mordred, The Wicked Day.<br /> <br /> Bernard Cornwell's <b>The Warlord Chronicles</b> (Winter King, Enemy of God, and Excalibur) are a good read, but try to stay very grounded in reality and Britain's immediate post-Roman history, including the idea of &quot;Arthur&quot; as a member of a Mithraic mystery cult. If anyone ever wondered what an Iron level take on Camelot for Scion might look like, it's good inspiration.<br /> <br /> TH White's <b>The Once and Future King</b> is also a good read, especially as you get to contrast Arthur as a kid verses as an adult. (Really, given Disney's recent obsession with remaking their animated films into big budget showcases - with mixed success - I'm kind of surprised trying to turn this into a Lord of the Rings style trilogy hasn't happened yet.)<br /> <br /> <b>Camelot 3000</b> was an early 80s comic miniseries by Mike W. Barr and Brian Bolland, in which Arthur awakens in the year 3000 to help defend Earth from an alien invasion. Several other characters are also returned, some in new incarnations, including Sir Triston (of Triston &amp; Isolde fame) now as a woman, with his-now-her relationship with the reborn (and still female) Isolde being part of the overall story arc.<br /> <br /> Other stuff that's good for ideas of about Arthur and company being reincarnated in the modern day include Matt Wagner's <i>Mage: The Hero Discovered</i>, Tim Powers's <i>The Drawing of the Dark</i>, Bernard Malamud's <i>The Natural</i> and its film adaption, Terry Gilliam's <i>The Fisher King</i>, and George Romero's <i>Knightriders</i>. And more strangely, the somewhat failed 90s cartoon/toy franchise <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Is1viI5yu8g\" target=\"_blank\">King Arthur &amp; The Knights of Justice</a>.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Sir Kay is my favorite Arthurian character, because in spite of his various flaws, he is fiercely and eternally loyal to his foster brother. The fact that there's a theory he may have originally been meant to be Cu Chulainn only makes him cooler in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T11:57:12-07:00","id":1413996,"title":"","content":"And if it salves anyone's conscience, MZB has been dead for a couple of decades. So, buying her books doesn't support her. (Hopefully the money goes to her daughter, if there's any justice in the world.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T12:09:12-07:00","id":1414002,"title":"","content":"Has anyone here read the delightful &quot;To the Chapel Perilous&quot;? It's not only a solid Arthurian fantasy it's a great satire on the press. You've got a Pict (he's painted blue) and a very &quot;Margret Murray&quot; witch who work for the British papers in an otherwise medieval Britain. The multiple aspects of the Grail are a major theme. Like Twain's &quot;Connecticut Yankee,&quot; the satire comes at you fast but then the story becomes dark and emotional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T12:13:14-07:00","id":1414003,"title":"","content":"I'd also bring up the Fate/ series from Japan (Fate/stay night, Fate/Grand Order, etc.), most famous for gender-flipping Arthur and Mordred (and Gareth), but also drawing on more of the high-powered supernatural elements from the original Arthurian works, and doing deep explorations of Camelot and its fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T12:22:27-07:00","id":1414009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1413996#post1413996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if it salves anyone's conscience, MZB has been dead for a couple of decades. So, buying her books doesn't support her. (Hopefully the money goes to her daughter, if there's any justice in the world.)</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of derailing the thread, why is everyone so certain she\u2019s guilty? I don\u2019t want to defend a child molester, but at the same time I don\u2019t want to condemn someone without evidence either.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not being inflammatory. If you have evidence that she\u2019s guilty, please let me know. I\u2019m just tryna figure out what happened. I read the Wikipedia page and the only evidence I could find was her daughter\u2019s accusations.<br /> <br /> To put it more bluntly: what do you guys know that I don\u2019t know that has you all convinced she\u2019s guilty? I\u2019m a lawyer irl (just starting out, but still a lawyer) and I clerked for a criminal court judge and I\u2019m reluctant to condemn anyone on the testimony of a single witness years after the fact.<br /> <br /> Again, sorry to derail the thread, but this has been bothering me for a while and I just want to know if I\u2019m defending the wrong person or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-16-2020, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:00:04-07:00","id":1414039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1414009#post1414009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it more bluntly: what do you guys know that I don\u2019t know that has you all convinced she\u2019s guilty? I\u2019m a lawyer irl (just starting out, but still a lawyer) and I clerked for a criminal court judge and I\u2019m reluctant to condemn anyone on the testimony of a single witness years after the fact..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of the book and don't know the situation that well so I&quot;m not going to comment on it specifically, but lets not conflate completely different standards of proof here. The criminal court standard of proof is drastically higher than the civil trial standard for a reason, because the ramifications are different (freedom vs money). Believing an accuser and choosing not to support an author accordingly is a very different ramification than locking someone in prison, and thus the standard of proof is lower.<br /> <br /> Rape and sexual abuse specifically often only have the testimony of the accuser as evidence, and I acknowledge that that often means justice demands the accused go free even when the liklihood is that they are guilty, because locking up the innocent is too great a risk if you aren't sure beyond all reasonable doubt. But if you are applying a &quot;preponderance of the evidence&quot; standard (which I think is fair when discussing social and financial ramifications rather than criminal conviction), then &quot;she said, she said&quot; just comes down to which claimant is, based on available information, more trustworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-17-2020, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:38:43-07:00","id":1414051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1413725-once-and-future-speculations?p=1414009#post1414009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of derailing the thread, why is everyone so certain she\u2019s guilty? I don\u2019t want to defend a child molester, but at the same time I don\u2019t want to condemn someone without evidence either.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">1:] Marion Zimmer Bradley confessed to knowing about her husband's pedophila and child rape during his trial.<br /> <br /> 2:] Her own daughter stated that Marion Zimmer Bradley sexually abused her. Moira Greyland also wrote a book on it (&quot;The Last Closet&quot;) that talks about how MZB used her fans to help her husband abuse children.<br /> <br /> As a note, there's no actual doubt about Marion Zimmer Bradley's guilt anymore than there is about David Eddings' child abuse. Please move on from this topic.<br /> <br /> It is a very trigger-filled subject and should be dealt with only with the best of care.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-16-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:39:13-07:00","id":1414052,"title":"","content":"The woman (MZB) is dead. Let whatever evil she did be buried with her. As for her books, if there is any good in them, enjoy them if you like. And, as someone said up thread, let the money go to those done wrong.<br /> <br /> Now, let's remember there is more than enough medieval Arthurian material, much of it with genuinely ancient matterials embedded in them, that discussing anything post-Mallory for any reason other than models for inclusion, is a waste of precious page space.<br /> <br /> On with the speculations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-18-2020, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:40:32-07:00","id":1414054,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No more mentioning MZB. Period.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:45:07-07:00","id":1414056,"title":"","content":"What do people think about Nikolai Tolstoy's work on Merlin? The Quest for Merlin.<br /> <br /> Amazon has it here. <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Quest-Merlin-Nikolai-Tolstoy/dp/0316850802/ref=sr_1_3?dchild=1&amp;keywords=nikolai+tolstoy&amp;qid=1600299731&amp;s=books&amp;sr=1-3\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/Quest-Merlin-...s=books&amp;sr=1-3</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-16-2020, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T16:43:17-07:00","id":1414090,"title":"","content":"I quite enjoyed Molly Cochran and Warren Murphy's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Forever_King\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Forev